{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented a new ambiguity-aware ladder policy in [optimal.py](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py).\n\nThe controller idea is: do a beta-scaled stage-1 scout pass, rank only the latest preview per live particle, keep extra survivors only when the score gap is small or uncertainty is high, then spend higher-beta budget on selective late confirmation and anchor-based backward children. The targeted weakness is the current mid/high-beta regime, especially `beta=0.5`, `0.75`, and `1.0`, where r0000 was at comparable NFE but still below the matched ODE baseline, and `beta=1.0` also left compute unused.\n\nI inspected:\n- `flow_tts_controller_implementation_spec.md`\n- the context-pack baseline target curve and recent frontier table\n- the beta-opportunity table\n- the borrowable strategy summary from `FlowEvo_10nobase/.../r0004/.../summary.json`\n- the r0000 compact summary at `history_autotts_b64_fixed_target_reference_20260527_051921/.../r0000/.../proposal_results/summary.json`\n- the r0000 controller snapshot and current [optimal.py](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py), which were identical\n- `flow_autotts/controllers/baselines.py`\n- `flow_autotts/core/state.py`\n- `flow_autotts/core/errors.py`\n- `flow_autotts/experiments/pickscore_sd35/env.py`\n\nThe exact beta schedule at the sweep points is:\n- `beta=0.00`, target `10`: deterministic single-root Euler finish only.\n- `beta=0.25`, target `20`: `2` roots, stage-1 preview at `t=0.3`, keep `1`, no backward children, early confirm `1`, late confirm `1`, tail previews `2`.\n- `beta=0.50`, target `36`: `3` roots, bounded SDE stage-1 scouts at `t=0.4`, keep `2`, early confirm `1`, late confirm `2`, `1` backward child from `t=0.8`, tail previews `3`.\n- `beta=0.75`, target `48`: `3` roots, bounded SDE scouts at `t=0.4`, keep `2` with keep-cap `3`, early confirm `2`, late confirm `2`, `2` backward children from `t=0.7`, tail previews `3`.\n- `beta=1.00`, target `64`: `4` roots, Euler scouts at `t=0.5`, keep `3`, early confirm `2`, late confirm `3`, `3` backward children from `t=0.6`, tail previews `5`.\n\nBudget use is monotonic because higher beta never reduces the target NFE curve, and it generally increases width, survivor count, confirmation slots, child count, and tail-confirmation allowance. `beta=1.0` cannot exceed `64` because every expensive action is gated by `_reserve(..., target_nfe)` and `target_nfe` is clamped to `min(env.budget, 64)`.\n\nBehaviorally new relative to the recent best controller:\n- it stops ranking all historical previews and instead ranks one latest preview per live particle, removing duplicate stale anchors from the decision loop;\n- it only re-previews when evidence is ambiguous or the particle state changed;\n- it adds a real two-stage ladder: scout, ambiguity-based survivor expansion, late confirmation, then selective backward refinement;\n- it uses bounded SDE only for mid-beta scouting, not as a blanket sampler.\n\nChecks I ran:\n- `python -m py_compile flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py`\n- a tiny fake-env dry run across `beta in {0.0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0}`\n\nExpected risks:\n- mid-beta SDE scouting could add noise without enough upside if PickScore prefers cleaner deterministic anchors;\n- low beta could still slightly underuse if early gaps are decisive and extra confirmation is not justified;\n- pruning after refinement is intentionally mild, so high-beta diversity may still cost reward-per-NFE if anchors are poor.\n\nPer-beta target-NFE reflection:\n- `beta=0.00`, target `10`: underuse is not an issue; locked deterministic policy is justified and unchanged.\n- `beta=0.25`, target `20`: mild underuse in the fake env looked unjustified, so I increased tail confirmation to improve utilization without adding backward branching.\n- `beta=0.50`, target `36`: previous weakness looked like poor allocation, not underuse; I shifted spend into multi-root scouting plus one selective child and confirmation. Fake dry-run hit `36`.\n- `beta=0.75`, target `48`: previous weakness looked like poor allocation near target; I kept target-level spend but made it evidence-driven with wider scout competition and two children.\n- `beta=1.00`, target `64`: previous underuse looked unjustified; I raised late confirmation/tail capacity so the policy can spend to the ceiling when ambiguity remains. Fake dry-run hit `64` exactly.\n\nThe matched baseline/frontier rows I used were:\n- baseline rewards at `(10, 20, 36, 48, 64)` NFE: `0.676462, 0.802083, 0.836650, 0.843990, 0.847290`\n- latest r0000 controller rows: `10/0.819160`, `20/0.828068`, `36/0.831124`, `48/0.839364`, `62.88/0.843137`\n\nThis proposal is meant to improve the weak `36`, `48`, and `64` regimes while protecting the already-strong `10` and `20` regimes."}}
