{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented a new controller in [optimal.py](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py).\n\n**Idea**\nThe controller is now a beta-scheduled preview tournament with two real new mechanisms.\n\n- It ranks only the latest preview per particle, so one branch cannot occupy multiple top slots with stale anchors.\n- It replaces same-state “confirmation previews” with ambiguity-triggered depth tournaments: if score gaps are small or drift/uncertainty is high, contenders are actually moved forward and previewed again at a later time.\n- At higher beta it keeps reserve branches, spends tail budget on either finishing a reserve or doing one more local backward refinement, and can explicitly commit the best `t=1` anchor by `backward(..., target_time=1.0, noise_policy=\"inferred_noise\")` before `answer(\"latest_active\")`.\n\nThat targets the current weak region: `beta=0.5/0.75/1.0`, especially `1.0`, where the incumbent trailed baseline and `r0001` showed that “more previews on the same states” was not the right repair.\n\n**What I inspected**\nI read the required files plus only targeted history named by the context pack:\n\n- [flow_tts_controller_implementation_spec.md](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/flow_tts_controller_implementation_spec.md)\n- [context_pack.md](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/logs/flow_autotts/pickscore_sd35/codex_logs_autotts_b64_fixed_target_reference_20260527_051921/r0002_20260527_051921_793d5c44/context_pack.md)\n- [flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py)\n- [flow_autotts/controllers/baselines.py](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/flow_autotts/controllers/baselines.py)\n- [r0000 optimal snapshot](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/logs/flow_autotts/pickscore_sd35/history_autotts_b64_fixed_target_reference_20260527_051921/r0000_20260527_051921_793d5c44/flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py)\n- [r0001 optimal snapshot](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/logs/flow_autotts/pickscore_sd35/history_autotts_b64_fixed_target_reference_20260527_051921/r0001_20260527_051921_793d5c44/flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py)\n- [r0001 summary](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/logs/flow_autotts/pickscore_sd35/history_autotts_b64_fixed_target_reference_20260527_051921/r0001_20260527_051921_793d5c44/proposal_results/summary.json)\n\nThe incumbent `r0000` frontier was:\n- `beta=0.00`: reward `0.819160`, mean NFE `10.0`\n- `beta=0.25`: reward `0.828068`, mean NFE `20.0`\n- `beta=0.50`: reward `0.831124`, mean NFE `36.0`\n- `beta=0.75`: reward `0.839364`, mean NFE `48.0`\n- `beta=1.00`: reward `0.843137`, mean NFE `62.88`\n\nAgainst the beta-matched ODE baseline, `0.00` and `0.25` were already above baseline; `0.50`, `0.75`, and `1.00` were below. `r0001` was a real behavior change, but its extra preview-heavy allocation still lost.\n\n**Beta Schedule**\nThe target-NFE curve stays exactly monotone by interpolation to `{0.0:10, 0.25:20, 0.5:36, 0.75:48, 1.0:64}` and every spending action is gated by `_reserve(..., target_nfe)`. Compute willingness also rises monotonically through roots, survivor width, tournament slots, reserve finishing, refinement count, and final commit behavior.\n\nExact schedule at the main sweep betas:\n\n- `beta=0.00`, target `10`: deterministic only, one root, no preview search, no refinement. This stays at the locked 10-NFE regime by a single full Euler finish.\n- `beta=0.25`, target `20`: `roots=2`, `warm_time=0.5`, `keep_floor=1`, `keep_cap=1`, `mid_tournament_slots=1`, `late_tournament_slots=0`, `max_children=0`, `tail_actions=1`, no commit. This is intentionally lightweight single-root selection with one possible ambiguity-resolving deepen.\n- `beta=0.50`, target `36`: `roots=3`, `warm_time=0.4`, `keep_floor=2`, `keep_cap=2`, `reserve_cap=1`, `mid_tournament_slots=1`, `late_tournament_slots=1`, `refine_time=0.8`, `max_children=1`, `finish_reserves=1`, `tail_actions=2`, no commit. This is the first real “tournament plus one selective child” regime.\n- `beta=0.75`, target `48`: `roots=3`, `warm_time=0.3`, `keep_floor=2`, `keep_cap=2`, `reserve_cap=1`, `mid_tournament_slots=2`, `late_tournament_slots=2`, `refine_time=0.7`, `max_children=2`, `max_refine_anchors=2`, `finish_reserves=1`, `tail_actions=3`, `commit_best=1`.\n- `beta=1.00`, target `64`: `roots=4`, `warm_time=0.3`, `keep_floor=2`, `keep_cap=3`, `reserve_cap=2`, `mid_tournament_slots=2`, `late_tournament_slots=3`, `refine_time=0.6`, `max_children=3`, `max_refine_anchors=2`, `finish_reserves=2`, `tail_actions=4`, `commit_best=1`.\n\nWhy monotone:\n- `target_nfe`, roots, reserve width, tournament slots, refinement count, tail actions, and commit activation are all nondecreasing with beta.\n- `refine_time` moves earlier as beta rises, so high beta spends more willingly on broader local exploration.\n- `beta=1.0` cannot exceed 64 because `_reserve` always caps at `min(env.budget, target_nfe)=64`, and the final `latest_active` path is only used after creating an explicit committed child at `t=1`, so it should incur no implicit forward.\n\n**Target-NFE Reflection**\nPer beta, relative to the injected targets:\n\n- `beta=0.00`, target `10`: underuse is not expected; deterministic finish should hit 10 exactly. No change needed.\n- `beta=0.25`, target `20`: likely around `18-20`. I adjusted upward versus a too-conservative single path by using two warm roots plus one ambiguity deepen. Any small residual underuse is justified if the second root is already clearly worse.\n- `beta=0.50`, target `36`: likely around `33-36`. I adjusted this regime upward with 3 warm roots, one reserve, one late tournament, one child, and optional reserve finish. Small leftover headroom is acceptable if only weak expensive actions remain.\n- `beta=0.75`, target `48`: likely around `46-48`. I adjusted upward with 2 tournament slots, 2 children, and final commit. Residual underuse should be justified rather than filled with duplicate previews.\n- `beta=1.00`, target `64`: likely around `62-64`. I adjusted upward with 4 roots, 3 late tournament slots, 2 reserve finishes, 3 children, and commit-best. It stays close to 64 while avoiding overshoot via reservation checks and zero-cost final commit before `latest_active`.\n\n**Checks**\n- `python -m py_compile flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py`\n- Lightweight dry-run on the toy `FlowTTSEnv`\n- Step-charging mock-env dry-run to approximate SD3.5 step costs; it produced monotone realized NFE of about `10, 18, 33, 46, 62`\n\nI did not run the full SD3.5 PickScore harness.\n\n**Expected Risks**\n- The final commit path assumes “commit latest best anchor” is better aligned than “best preview ever”; if preview ranking is already sufficient, gains may be modest.\n- `beta=0.50` is the main intended repair, but if it still trails baseline, the remaining issue is probably branch quality rather than pure underuse.\n- High-beta reserve keeping is gentler than the incumbent, so if diversity is mostly noise, `0.75/1.0` could spend some budget on weaker contenders."}}
