{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented a new margin-aware tournament controller in [optimal.py](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py).\n\nThe idea is: warm-preview a small root pool, keep top survivors plus beta-scaled reserves, then spend compute in a stricter order than the incumbent: early warm-stage reserve promotion if the warm gap is still close or uncertain, finish survivors, rescue unfinished challengers only when latest evidence remains ambiguous, then use completed-anchor backward refinement and tail confirmations. That targets the main weak region from the context pack: `beta=0.5/0.75/1.0` trailing the beta-matched ODE baseline, with `beta=1.0` also underusing compute.\n\nI inspected:\n- [flow_tts_controller_implementation_spec.md](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/flow_tts_controller_implementation_spec.md)\n- [context_pack.md](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/logs/flow_autotts/pickscore_sd35/codex_logs_autotts_b64_fixed_target_reference_20260527_051921/r0004_20260527_051921_793d5c44/context_pack.md)\n- [optimal.py](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py)\n- [baselines.py](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/flow_autotts/controllers/baselines.py)\n- [r0000 optimal snapshot](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/logs/flow_autotts/pickscore_sd35/history_autotts_b64_fixed_target_reference_20260527_051921/r0000_20260527_051921_793d5c44/flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py)\n- [r0000 summary](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/logs/flow_autotts/pickscore_sd35/history_autotts_b64_fixed_target_reference_20260527_051921/r0000_20260527_051921_793d5c44/proposal_results/summary.json)\n- [r0001 optimal snapshot](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/logs/flow_autotts/pickscore_sd35/history_autotts_b64_fixed_target_reference_20260527_051921/r0001_20260527_051921_793d5c44/flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py)\n- [r0002 optimal snapshot](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/logs/flow_autotts/pickscore_sd35/history_autotts_b64_fixed_target_reference_20260527_051921/r0002_20260527_051921_793d5c44/flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py)\n- [r0003 optimal snapshot](/inspire/hdd/global_user/gongjingjing-25039/sywang/jkcai/FlowEvo/logs/flow_autotts/pickscore_sd35/history_autotts_b64_fixed_target_reference_20260527_051921/r0003_20260527_051921_793d5c44/flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py)\n\nLatest compact history from the context pack:\n- `beta=0.0`: reward `0.819160`, mean NFE `10.0`, beats baseline `0.676462`\n- `beta=0.25`: reward `0.828068`, mean NFE `20.0`, beats baseline `0.802083`\n- `beta=0.5`: reward `0.831124`, mean NFE `36.0`, trails baseline `0.836650`\n- `beta=0.75`: reward `0.839364`, mean NFE `48.0`, trails baseline `0.843990`\n- `beta=1.0`: reward `0.843137`, mean NFE `62.88`, trails baseline `0.847290`\n\nThe last two proposal snapshots were real behavioral changes, not comment churn: `r0002` added tournament/commit logic and shifted budget from preview into more forward/backward, while `r0003` added reserve rescue and late search. Both were rejected, and the compact lessons point to the same failure mode: under-target spending at `beta=0.75/1.0`, plus one case where extra previews at `beta=1.0` did not help. The incumbent/current accepted controller was identical to `r0000`.\n\nExact beta schedule:\n- Target NFE is interpolated from `{0.0:10, 0.25:20, 0.5:36, 0.75:48, 1.0:64}` and always capped by `env.budget`.\n- `beta=0`: deterministic only.\n- Roots: `1` if `<0.18`, `2` if `<0.45`, `3` if `<0.9`, else `4`.\n- Warm preview time: `0.5` if `<0.35`, `0.4` if `<0.8`, else `0.3`.\n- Survivor floor: `1` if `<0.45`, else `2`.\n- Survivor cap: `1` if `<0.35`, `2` if `<0.85`, else `3`.\n- Reserve cap: `0` if `<0.45`, `1` if `<0.85`, else `2`.\n- Warm reserve promotions: `0` if `<0.45`, `1` if `<0.8`, else `2`.\n- Challenger rescues after survivor completion: `0` if `<0.45`, `1` if `<0.85`, else `2`.\n- Extra active finisher slots: `0` if `<0.45`, `1` if `<0.8`, else `2`.\n- Confirmation slots: `0` if `<0.3`, `1` if `<0.55`, `2` if `<0.9`, else `3`.\n- Backward children: `0` if `<0.45`, `1` if `<0.7`, `2` if `<0.9`, else `3`.\n- Backward target time: `0.84` if `<0.45`, `0.74` if `<0.8`, else `0.62`.\n- Tail preview budget: `1` if `<0.3`, `2` if `<0.55`, `3` if `<0.9`, else `4`.\n\nThat is monotone in willingness to spend: higher beta gets more roots, more reserves, more reserve promotions, more challenger completions, more confirmations, more backward children, earlier backward targets, and more tail spend. Every spending path is guarded by `_reserve(...)`, so `beta=1.0` cannot exceed `64`.\n\nBehaviorally new relative to the recent best:\n- The incumbent did warm preview, immediate pruning, finish survivors, then generic confirm/refine/fill. It had no explicit “promote unfinished warm reserve before completed branches dominate the ranking” mechanism.\n- This proposal adds warm-stage reserve promotion plus later challenger completion, both triggered by score gap and uncertainty.\n- It also shifts tail spending priority toward useful unfinished challengers before duplicate confirmation, which directly addresses the context-pack underuse warnings without repeating the rejected “just add more previews” pattern.\n\nChecks run:\n- `python -m py_compile flow_autotts/controllers/optimal.py`\n- tiny fake-env dry run across betas\n\nFake-env dry-run NFE usage:\n- `beta=0.0 -> 10`\n- `beta=0.25 -> 19`\n- `beta=0.5 -> 36`\n- `beta=0.75 -> 47`\n- `beta=1.0 -> 64`\n\nTarget-NFE reflection:\n- `beta=0.0`, target `10`: underuse is not allowed by schedule; controller is deterministic and should land exactly at the locked 10. This is justified because low-beta search would just waste reward/NFE.\n- `beta=0.25`, target `20`: the policy is still intentionally conservative. Slight underuse is acceptable here because this regime already beats baseline and the rejected history showed that low-beta under-target usage can regress reward. I left it near the incumbent behavior.\n- `beta=0.5`, target `36`: this was a weak regime at matched NFE. I adjusted the policy to improve utilization via warm reserve promotion and one challenger finish slot; fake-env hits `36`.\n- `beta=0.75`, target `48`: this was weak and prior rejected rounds underspent. I adjusted the policy to spend more meaningfully with reserve promotion, one extra active finisher, more confirmations, and up to two backward children; fake-env reaches `47`, which is close without overshoot.\n- `beta=1.0`, target `64`: this was weak and under target at `62.88`. I adjusted the policy most strongly here with four roots, two reserves, two reserve promotions, two extra active finisher slots, three confirm slots, and three children; fake-env reaches `64`. Exceeding `64` is avoided because every expensive action is pre-checked by `_reserve(...)` against `min(env.budget, target_nfe)`.\n\nExpected risks:\n- Repeated same-state `preview` confirmations may still have limited marginal value if PickScore noise is low; the hedge is that they only happen after challenger completion/refinement opportunities are considered.\n- Warm reserve promotion could over-spend on mediocre branches if warm previews are especially noisy at `t=0.3/0.4`; that risk is why low beta keeps reserve promotion off and high beta requires close-gap or uncertainty evidence.\n- Backward refinement remains completion-only and anchored to close finalists; if local perturbations are too weak, gains may come mostly from better challenger allocation rather than refinement itself.\n\nThe intended improvement target is `beta=0.5` first, then `beta=0.75` and `beta=1.0`, while preserving the already-strong `beta=0` and `beta=0.25`."}}
